  <p class="app-title">Appendix III</p>
  <p class="app-subtitle" style="margin-bottom:12px;">Financial Aid and Scholarships</p>

  <p class="para">Students are admitted to NLSIU based on their academic performance in the admission process. The University has adopted an inclusion policy that ensures that students from diverse social, linguistic and economic backgrounds from across India benefit from a rigorous and transformative education. The admission process does not take into account the financial background of the applicant. Student fees for on-campus academic programmes cover only part of the actual cost of education, with the University subsidising the remaining cost. Further, the University is dedicated to ensuring that students admitted to an academic programme are provided with necessary support to continue their studies, irrespective of financial constraints. The <a href="https://www.nls.ac.in/information/students/financial-aid-for-students/financial-aid-policy/" style="font-weight:700; color:#900;">Financial Aid Policy</a> sets out the University's approach to delivering on this commitment.</p>

  <p class="para">Students whose gross family income is less than Rs. 8,00,000 per annum are eligible to apply for financial aid by the university. Before submitting their application for University's financial aid, candidates <strong>must</strong> apply under the <strong>PM Vidyalaxmi Scheme</strong>. NLSIU has been recognised by the Government of India under the PM-Vidyalaxmi Scheme as one of the leading higher educational institutions in the country. The PM Vidyalaxmi Scheme provides collateral-free and guarantor-free education loans to meritorious students in top institutions in India. There is no income limit to apply for this scheme, and loans up to Rs. 30 lakhs can be availed. Partial and full interest subvention is available for lower annual family incomes.</p>

  <p class="para">The application to PM Vidyalaxmi Scheme must be filled through the official PM Vidyalaxmi Portal: <span style="font-weight:700; color:#900; text-decoration:underline;">https://pmvidyalaxmi.co.in</span> before applying for financial aid with the University. For detailed guidelines &amp; process, please visit <span style="font-weight:700; color:#900; text-decoration:underline;">PM Vidyalaxmi Scheme</span> section of the universities scholarship page. A copy of the education loan application must be submitted along with the application for university financial aid. This is a pre-condition for applying for financial aid through the University. In the absence of this document, the financial aid process will be kept in abeyance.</p>

  <p class="para">Candidates who wish to apply for financial assistance under the University's Financial Aid Policy are required to submit their application for financial aid on or before {{ financial_aid_deadline }}. The University will communicate its decision on the financial aid applications by {{ var_fin_aid_decision_date }}. Students who are provided financial aid shall have their fee reimbursed up to the extent of the aid provided. Application for financial aid does not exempt you from payment of the full fees before {{ full_fee_deadline }}.</p>

  <p class="para">Students who have been admitted to NLSIU may also be eligible for a number of scholarships sponsored by the central and state governments as well as private organisations. NLSIU has curated a <span style="font-weight:700; color:#900; text-decoration:underline;">list of some such scholarships</span> for the benefit of candidates. Students may also visit the <span style="font-weight:700; color:#900; text-decoration:underline;">National Scholarship Portal</span> for more information. For further assistance in this regard, please contact <span style="font-weight:700; color:#900; text-decoration:underline;">nlsiuscholarship@nls.ac.in</span>.</p>
</div>

