  <div class="faq-block">
    <p class="faq-q">41. How do I apply for University residence?</p>
    <p class="faq-a">When accepting the offer in the admissions portal, you will be asked whether you wish to apply for accommodation. Select "Yes" if you want to apply. The housing fee will then be added to your fee invoice.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="faq-block">
    <p class="faq-q">42. Can I choose not to apply for University residence?</p>
    <p class="faq-a">Yes. Select "No" in the portal if you do not want to apply for University accommodation. You may then independently arrange private accommodation.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="faq-block">
    <p class="faq-q">43. If I select "Yes", when must I pay the housing fee?</p>
    <p class="faq-a">If you select "Yes", the full housing fee of Rs. {{ housing_fee }} will be included in your fee invoice and must be paid by {{ full_fee_deadline }} along with the balance fee.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="faq-block">
    <p class="faq-q">44. Can NLSIU help me find private housing?</p>
    <p class="faq-a">No. Students may independently explore private hostels, paying guest facilities, or rental housing around Nagarbhavi depending on their budget and convenience. We encourage students who do not have housing in Bengaluru, to come to Bengaluru early to identify suitable options.</p>
